 "note": "Per-(month,model) token cells produced by `npx ccusage@latest monthly --breakdown --json` on 2026-09-12, one run per box with CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR pointed at that box's claude-projects. Numbers and model ids only: no transcript path and no message content. Boxes are keyed by `usage::box_key`, an FNV-1a digest of the box name, and NOT by the name: a real box name is fleet residue that `tools/residue-check.py` refuses to let into the tree (SKEIN-629). The test hashes the directory names it finds at run time to match these rows, so it can still print the real name of any box it disagrees with. `fingerprint` is (file count, total bytes, newest mtime in whole seconds) for that box's transcripts when the cells were last confirmed; a box whose transcripts have since moved cannot be held to these numbers and the test says so rather than failing. `excluded` holds the boxes that could not be confirmed at all, each with the evidence for why its cells are not reachable from the bytes that are there now; the fleet-size test counts them so one cannot be dropped quietly."
}